# OS/7 — console font for the installed system in non-GUI mode.
#
# Decision D15 (installer/SETUP-PLAN.md §2.8): CASCADIA MONO for the installed
# console. Decision D9 (§2.3) keeps Fixedsys Excelsior for os7-setup, which is a
# deliberate MS-DOS 6.22 / Windows 2000 reproduction and needs the period face.
# Setup calls setfont with its own PSF before it paints, so this file governs
# the installed console only.
#
# Both fonts are in /usr/share/consolefonts beside this file:
#
#   os7-console-*.psf.gz     Cascadia Mono  <- selected below
#   os7-fixedsys-*.psf.gz    Fixedsys Excelsior, what Setup uses
#
# To put the installer's face on the installed console, change FONT below to
# os7-fixedsys-16x32.psf.gz. Nothing else has to move.
#
# The PSFs are built from pinned sources by build/lib/build-console-font.sh and
# build/lib/build-installed-console-font.sh; the toolchain that makes them lives
# in the build container and never ships here.
#
# CASCADIA IS OFL 1.1, NOT CC0. Its licence ships at
# /usr/share/doc/os7-console-font/LICENSE and must stay with the font. The PSF
# is deliberately not named after the font: OFL treats a format change as a
# Modified Version, which may not carry the reserved name "Cascadia Code".
#
# WHY FONT= AND NOT FONTFACE/FONTSIZE: setupcon composes a filename out of
# CODESET+FONTFACE+FONTSIZE and would go looking for a Debian-named font that
# does not exist. FONT= is taken verbatim (setupcon line ~642), which is what a
# font from outside the distribution needs.
#
# WHY 16x32 IS THE DEFAULT: 8x16 on a 1920x1080 panel is a 240x67 grid - legible
# only in the sense that the pixels are there. 16x32 gives 120x33.
#
# For Cascadia the large cell is a SECOND RASTERISATION, not a pixel doubling:
# it is an outline font, so 16x32 carries twice the detail rather than twice the
# pixel size. (Fixedsys's 16x32 is doubled, because a bitmap face has no more
# detail to give.) os7-console-8x16.psf.gz is installed alongside for small
# framebuffers and for serial/rescue use; swap the name below to switch.
#
# console-setup applies this FROM THE INITRAMFS (FRAMEBUFFER=y), i.e. before the
# root filesystem is mounted, so only the earliest boot frames use the kernel's
# built-in font. That gap is L20 and it is a few frames wide.

ACTIVE_CONSOLES="/dev/tty[1-6]"

CHARMAP="UTF-8"

# Deliberately empty: FONT below supersedes them. Leaving FONTFACE="Fixed"
# behind would make setupcon try to be helpful on top of an explicit choice.
CODESET=
FONTFACE=
FONTSIZE=

FONT="os7-console-16x32.psf.gz"

VIDEOMODE=
